  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.0.3:\n- The documentation and the changelog of each release are on GitHub, with a release for each version: https://github.com/Abstractions-AS/sass-compiler (the source is not there). The package names it as its repository, and the Visual Studio extension links to it.\n2.0.1 and 2.0.2, fixes since 2.0.0:\n- Compressed CSS with a character outside ASCII (an icon font, Bulma 1.0) was written with two byte order marks, so a browser dropped its first rule, such as the @font-face of the icons. It has one now. Delete such a CSS file, or save sassconfig.json, and build, to write it again.\n- On Windows, a new CSS file, its source map and its folders were named in lower case (wwwroot/Css/DatePickers.css became wwwroot/css/datepickers.css), which a case-sensitive file system (Linux, Docker) does not find by its name. They are named as sassconfig.json names them now. Rename a file that is in lower case once (in git, git mv -f).\n2.0.0:\n- LibSass, the default, fails with an error on @use and @forward, which it wrote to the CSS without an error, so the CSS was broken. A build that passed with such a file fails: set \"runtime\": \"DartSass\" for it in sassconfig.json.\n- Visual Studio: Initialize with sets up an ASP.NET Core or Blazor project with an empty Sass file, Bulma, Bootstrap or Pico CSS (downloaded with LibMan); Add icon font adds Font Awesome, Material Symbols or Bootstrap Icons, with a CopyWebFonts target that copies their fonts to wwwroot/fonts; Cleanup VS template moves what the ASP.NET Core templates put in wwwroot to the Recycle Bin.",
